From 412e430ccd8772a39da3efd6df6e704c80b2d8b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolzen <funer@gmx.at>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:10:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] manager/user: Recognise callers from a game without systemd

A sender counted as a game when its cgroup was an app-steam-app scope,
which steam-launch-wrapper creates through systemd. Without systemd, as on
runit systems, there is no such scope, but Steam still starts the game
through its reaper (reaper SteamLaunch), which as a subreaper keeps every
process of the game below it. On runit a sender with that reaper among its
ancestors is now refused as well. systemd systems are unchanged.
---
 steamos-manager/src/manager/user.rs | 128 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 126 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

